within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.C_CardiovascularSystem.C07A_BetaBlockingAgents.C07AA05_Propranolol;
model Propranolol "Propranolol — default model: Propranolol_Salehifar2017_mean_of_differences"
  extends Propranolol_Salehifar2017_mean_of_differences;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of propranolol: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.C_CardiovascularSystem.C07A_BetaBlockingAgents.C07AA05_Propranolol.Propranolol_Salehifar2017_mean_of_differences\">Propranolol_Salehifar2017_mean_of_differences</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of propranolol in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Propranolol_Salehifar2017_mean_of_differences</code></li><li><code>Propranolol_Salehifar2017_other_sources</code></li><li><code>Propranolol_Salehifar2017_this_study</code></li><li><code>Propranolol_Takechi2018_reference</code></li></ul><h4>About propranolol</h4><p>Propranolol is a non-selective beta blocker used for conditions such as high blood pressure, angina, heart rhythm problems, migraine, anxiety, essential tremor, and infantile hemangioma. It remains widely used, is listed among WHO essential medicines, and is authorised in the European Union, where an approved product is indicated for hemangioma.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q423364\">Wikidata Q423364</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Propranolol\">Propranolol</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>10/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 86400, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Propranolol;
